proof.text:
For coefficient maps $v:Lh^*K\to K$ and $w:Lg^*K\to K$, the coefficient map for the ordered composite $h\circ g$ is $w\circ Lg^*v:Lg^*Lh^*K\to K$. Naturality of $q_g$ (Step 2, applied to the underlying map $v:Lh^*K\to K$) and the equation of Step 4 give
$$\begin{aligned}
T_{g,w}\circ T_{h,v}
 &=H(w)\circ q_{g,K}\circ H(v)\circ q_{h,K}\\
 &=H(w)\circ H(Lg^*v)\circ q_{g,Lh^*K}\circ q_{h,K}\\
 &=H(w\circ Lg^*v)\circ q_{h\circ g,K}
 =T_{h\circ g,w\circ Lg^*v}.
\end{aligned}$$
The identity pair has identity operator by Step 4. For three endomorphisms, the two parenthesizations give the same composite of the three operators by associativity, with the coefficient maps identified by the coherent pullback composition comparisons used in Step 4. This proves composition compatibility with its order and identity specified.
